# BLUEPRINT:BEGIN — blueprint-managed. Put YOUR guards below the end marker.
#
# Everything between the markers is owned by the blueprint and is REPLACED by
# `blueprint pull`; everything below the end marker is yours and is preserved
# byte-for-byte (marker_aware_merge, scripts/blueprint.mts). Editing inside the
# region means losing the edit at the next pull — back-propagate it instead:
# `blueprint a2bp .githooks/pre-push-project`.
#
# THE PROSE ABOVE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT SPELL THE END MARKER (BUG-052).
# marker_aware_merge counts the marker tokens as SUBSTRINGS and refuses to merge
# unless BEGIN and END balance. Two sentences here mentioned the end token by
# name, giving this file a count of 1 and 3 — so the merge never ran, `pull`
# fell back to a whole-file copy, and every derived project's own guards below
# the region were REPLACED on every pull. The guarantee stated in this very
# paragraph was broken by the paragraph stating it. tests/manifest #7b now
# asserts the balance on both managed files.
#
# It is managed because it MUST travel with tests/ (BUG-029). A suite is
# coherent only as two things — the files, and its invocation here. (It used to
# be three; TASK-020 deleted tests/SUITES.md, whose row was a second description
# of what those two already say.) Sync the suites without the wiring and
# `tests/manifest` #4 fails every push on a suite the gate cannot invoke; sync
# the wiring without the suites and the gate is armed over nothing, which is
# BUG-004 and A-22 in a new costume.
#
# Sourced by .githooks/pre-push (see its "Project-specific guards" section).
# The generic hook runs build/lint/test per workspace; the stages below run the
# regression suites that guard the blueprint-managed machinery this project
# depends on (blueprint pull/drift/a2bp, signal-set.sh, the feed, the hooks,
# the gate renderer). Without them a regression to any of it pushes green —
# audit finding A-15.
#
# There is NO wall-clock ceiling (founder decision 2026-08-02 closing BUG-005;
# docs/DoD.md §3). The gate reports its total and slowest
# stage every run. Suites named `*.release.spec.ts` run in CI only (TASK-054),
# and the vitest stage prints a skip line for each.

# Normally sourced by .githooks/pre-push, which has already sourced the renderer
# and called pipe_init. Sourcing defensively keeps this file runnable on its own
# (and keeps the "every gate file wires to the one renderer" assertion honest)
# without starting a second pipeline inside the parent's.
# shellcheck source=scripts/lib/pipeline.sh
#
# BUG-066: every path in this file hangs off $BP_CODE_ROOT, which the parent
# hook resolves from git-guaranteed cwd. The `.` default keeps this file
# runnable on its own and is what the cwd-relative form used to mean.
: "${BP_CODE_ROOT:=.}"
command -v pipe_stage >/dev/null 2>&1 || . "$BP_CODE_ROOT/scripts/lib/pipeline.sh"

